      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes #63057\n\n`Worker.sleep` no longer asserts that device-wide free memory did not drop. It logs a warning instead.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `/sleep` no longer returns a 500 when another process allocates on the same GPU during the sleep window.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew CPU-only test `test_worker_sleep_tolerates_other_processes_using_device_memory` in `tests/v1/worker/test_sleep_mode_backend.py` mocks `torch.accelerator.get_memory_info` so free memory drops from 10 GiB to 8 GiB across `sleep()`.\n\n- Before the fix: fails with `AssertionError: Memory usage increased after sleeping.`\n- After the fix: passes, along with the other 9 tests in the file.\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on both files.\n\nRun with `pytest tests/v1/worker/test_sleep_mode_backend.py --noconftest` (CPU torch, Python 3.12). Not run on a GPU, not run end to end with two real processes.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py` compared `torch.accelerator.get_memory_info()` (device-wide) before and after suspend and asserted `freed_bytes >= 0`. That includes other processes' allocations.\n\nI took the warning option from the issue. Per-process accounting from the allocator was left out as a larger change. The existing ROCm retry loop is unchanged.\n\nThanks to @zenedgex for the report.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>",
